course: dictionary
lesson: 6764
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The word «operating» is a good example. Its meaning depends on the words around it, which are its context. «The shop's operating hours are nine till five.» Here operating means working or open for business, because the hours are when the shop is open.
explain: «The vet is operating on the frog's leg.» Now operating means cutting into a body to fix it. The words vet, frog and leg are the clues. When you meet a word with more than one meaning, ask: what is the topic of this sentence? A hospital, a shop, a computer or a maths sum? The topic tells you which meaning to use.
explain: Always check your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the hard word. «The machine is operating normally» makes sense with working in place of operating. «The machine is cutting into a body normally» does not make sense, so that meaning is wrong here.
fact: Operating can mean working or running, said of a machine or a business.
fact: Operating can also mean making a machine work or controlling it.
fact: Operating can mean doing a medical operation, cutting into a body to fix it.
fact: An operating system is the program that runs a computer, and an operating theatre (UK) or operating room (US) is where doctors operate on patients.
fact: «Operating» can also mean using an operation like adding or multiplying in maths.
exercise: «Big zoos have hospitals with X-ray machines, scanners, labs and operating rooms.» What is an operating room? | *A room for doctors to cut into patients | A room for playing games | A room where the zoo keeper sleeps | A room where doctors do operations
exercise: Tom says, «The shop's operating hours are nine till five.» What does operating mean? | *Working or open for business | Adding and multiplying numbers | Cutting into a body to fix it | Painting the walls
exercise: What does an operating system do? | *Runs the computer | Cuts into a body | Stops the rain | Cooks food for the computer
test: «The machine is operating normally.» What does operating mean here? | Painted bright red | Broken forever | *Working properly | Sleeping
test: «The vet is operating on the frog's leg.» What does operating mean here? | *Cutting into the body to fix it | Painting a picture | Running a race | Counting coins
exam: In «operating hours», what does operating mean? | *Working or open for business | Cutting into a body | Hiding under a table | Adding numbers
